WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:15.490
Inside onlineAttention, next is the new maximum score found for the tile. expf(x) computes the exponential of an FP32 value; it supplies the rescaling factor and weights. denominator and weighted carry the running totals.

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:22.730
This correctness example uses one GPU thread over eight keys; it is not a parallel FlashAttention implementation.

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:25.905
Find tile maximum.

00:00:25.905 --> 00:00:28.440
Compare scores with the running maximum.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:29.895
Rescale and add.

00:00:29.895 --> 00:00:32.690
Carry a denominator and weighted sum forward.

00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:33.740
Normalise.

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:36.625
Divide after processing all key tiles.

00:00:38.125 --> 00:00:42.955
Running totals can remain as thread working state while successive key and value tiles are read.

00:00:42.955 --> 00:00:46.625
Avoiding a full score array changes intermediate storage.

00:00:46.625 --> 00:00:52.900
Real parallel attention kernels also use shared memory and matrix units according to their implementation.
